.0296]},{"n":"Yumemizuki Mizuki","r":[0.0815,0.7496,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Diona","r":[0.1704,0.7496,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Sucrose","r":[0.2148,0.7496,0.037,0.0296]}]}]}},"thumb":"content/genshin/builds/yumemizukimizuki/261111-225430/en-1.t.webp","why":{"w":[{"name":"Sunny Morning Sleep-In","text":"Signature EM catalyst gaining more EM through Swirl, Skill hits and Burst hits."},{"name":"Reliquary of Truth","text":"Strong CRIT-oriented catalyst with bonuses for its intended reaction and team setup."},{"name":"A Thousand Floating Dreams","text":"Provides 265 EM at Level 90, up to 30% Elemental DMG Bonus from diverse teammates, and 40 teamwide EM at R1, boosting Mizuki’s Swirl damage and team reactions."},{"name":"The Widsith","text":"Provides 55.1% CRIT DMG and a random ATK, Elemental DMG, or EM buff, offering strong but inconsistent damage boosts for Mizuki."},{"name":"Favonius Codex","text":"High Energy Recharge and particle generation keep the burst ready on demand."},{"name":"Fruit of Fulfillment","text":"Provides 45.9% Energy Recharge and increases EM after using an Elemental Reaction, making it a solid F2P option for Mizuki’s Swirl damage and Burst uptime."},{"name":"Hakushin Ring","text":"When Mizuki triggers an Electro-related reaction, she can increase elemental damage for the participating elements."},{"name":"Etherlight Spindlelute","text":"Energy Recharge event catalyst; helps meet Burst needs where personal damage is secondary."}],"a":[{"names":["Gilded Dreams"],"text":"Strong EM-focused set for Swirl and competitive Stellar Swirl damage; best when reaction uptime is consistent.","stats":"EM · EM · CR/CD"},{"names":["Scarlet Proof"],"text":"Stellar Swirl option: grants 16% CRIT Rate and 40% Stellar Swirl DMG after triggering it. The 2pc ATK is less useful.","stats":""},{"names":["Wanderer's Troupe","Gilded Dreams"],"text":"Two EM bonuses grant 160 EM. A flexible fallback for Stellar Swirl or traditional Swirl builds.","stats":""}],"t":[{"name":"Wind Chill Factor","members":["Yumemizuki Mizuki","Odette","Vodyanitsa","Faruzan"],"text":"Mizuki drives on-field Swirl damage, Odette enables Stellar Swirl and provides Cryo support, Vodyanitsa heals and shreds RES, and Faruzan buffs Anemo damage and shreds Anemo RES.","roles":["Main DPS","Stellar","Support","Res Shred"]},{"name":"Swirl Problems","members":["Yumemizuki Mizuki","Traveler (Cryo)","qiqi","Faruzan"],"text":"Mizuki drives on-field Swirl damage, Cryo Traveler provides off-field Cryo application, Qiqi heals and adds Cryo support, and Faruzan buffs Anemo damage and shreds Anemo RES.","roles":["Main DPS","Stellar","Support","Res Shred"]},{"name":"Lunar-tics","members":["Yumemizuki Mizuki","Columbina","Ineffa","Sucrose"],"text":"Mizuki drives on-field Swirl damage, Columbina buffs Lunar reactions, Ineffa provides off-field Electro and Lunar-Charged damage, and Sucrose boosts EM and shreds RES.","roles":["Main DPS","Lunar","Support","EM Build"]},{"name":"Discount Draft","members":["Yumemizuki Mizuki","Traveler (Cryo)","Diona","Sucrose"],"text":"Mizuki drives Swirl damage, Cryo Traveler provides off-field Cryo application, Diona shields and heals, and Sucrose boosts EM and shreds RES.","roles":["Main DPS","Stellar","Support","EM Build"]}],"v":"Stellar Swirl DPS: Use a Cryo enabler. Build EM/EM/CRIT; Scarlet Proof adds CRIT and Stellar Swirl damage.\nTraditional Swirl: Use triple EM with Gilded or Viridescent Venerer. Standard Swirl does not CRIT.","n":4},"seo":{"roles":["Main DPS"],"about":"Mizuki drives Swirl and Stellar Swirl from the field. Stellar Swirl can CRIT, favoring EM plus CRIT; traditional Swirl favors EM and ER instead. Her Burst also provides healing.","pros":["Strong Stellar Swirl DMG","Excellent team support","Built-in healing","Great AoE potential"],"cons":["Needs high EM investment","Limited team flexibility","Requires Cryo/SSW enablers"],"weapons":["Sunny Morning Sleep-In","Reliquary of Truth","A Thousand Floating Dreams","The Widsith","Favonius Codex",